                <pb facs="0129" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/1340: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-09T12:00:00-04:00">May 9, 1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 9—11:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. From Braden. Finot has been appointed Bolivian first assistant replacing
                    Alvestegui temporarily until another appointment is made. He assured me last
                    night of complete cooperation along the lines Conference is now pursuing.</p>
                <p>Saturday afternoon mediators demanded that the Paraguayan delegation now submit
                    last word on Saturday.</p>
                <p>I am endeavoring to get invitations issued to ex-belligerent Foreign Ministers
                    within the next few days so that their arrival may coincide with that of Chilean
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs on May 19. Brazilian delegate tells me Brazilian
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs also will come here if his presence is deemed
                    desirable. [Braden.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
